{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And you shall make.</b> Any shape whose length equals its width is called a square, and this one is a square in cubits, for there are five shapes that are quadrilaterals:" "Now if we say that a ramp is unnecessary, as our predecessors said, because its height is three cubits — then what will the deniers do with the altar that Solomon made, whose height was ten cubits, while a man's height is only four cubits?" "<b>And the sense of \"square.\"</b> Because the length is like the width:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:38.814517452Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}